# Trivy CVE suppression list — CryptoClaw monorepo image.
#
# Per ADR-0016: the trivy gate fails on CRITICAL severity with --ignore-unfixed.
# Suppressions here are exceptions to that gate, each with explicit OpenVEX-style
# justification and an expiration that forces re-evaluation.
#
# Format: <CVE-ID> exp:<YYYY-MM-DD>
# Reviewers: every entry MUST have a comment block above it documenting:
#   - vulnerable component + version
#   - why the runtime image is not affected today
#   - the permanent fix path and which phase resolves it
#   - the OpenVEX justification (not_affected | affected | fixed | under_investigation)
# When in doubt, ship the upstream fix instead of adding an entry here.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-6270 — @fastify/middie 8.3.3 middleware auth bypass in child plugin scopes
#
# Component:        @fastify/middie@8.3.3 (transitive via @nestjs/platform-fastify@10.4.22)
# Fixed in:         @fastify/middie@9.3.2
# Why suppressed:   middie's vulnerable code path is the Express-style middleware
#                   plugin pipeline. Our image registers ZERO middleware — there
#                   are no @Controller() classes (P0a/P0b have no HTTP routes
#                   beyond the global '/v1' prefix), no app.use() calls in
#                   bootstrap(), and no auth middleware until P1+. The auth-bypass
#                   pre-condition (a registered middleware with child plugin scope)
#                   does not exist at runtime.
# Permanent fix:    middie 9.x requires Fastify 5.x, which requires NestJS 11.
#                   NestJS 10 → 11 upgrade is tracked for P3 (when controllers
#                   land) or the P6 hardening pass — whichever comes first. At
#                   that point this entry is removed and the gate validates the
#                   patched dep tree.
# Reachability:     verified by `grep -RE "@Controller\(|app\.use" apps/ libs/` — empty.
# OpenVEX status:   not_affected
# OpenVEX justification: vulnerable_code_not_in_execute_path
# Re-evaluate by:   2026-09-01 (forces a check before the 4-month mark; if NestJS 11
#                   bump hasn't shipped by then, decide whether to extend or escalate).
CVE-2026-6270 exp:2026-09-01
